0:["y07uMnhZvjRDJDyCaG9hS",[[["",{"children":["(workspace)",{"children":["learning",{"children":["strategy",{"children":[["id","expiry-architecture","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"id\":\"expiry-architecture\"}",{}]}]}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["(workspace)",{"children":["learning",{"children":["strategy",{"children":[["id","expiry-architecture","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-[820px] space-y-4 p-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/learning","className":"text-[11px] font-semibold text-teal hover:underline","children":"← All lessons"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-text","children":"NSE and BSE Expiry Architecture"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-bold leading-tight whitespace-nowrap bg-hover text-muted border border-border2 px-1.5 py-0 text-[9px]","children":"beginner"}],false]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-muted","children":"Which contracts expire on which day, why only two indices still carry weekly expiries, and how the holiday rule shifts settlement."}]]}],false,["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"NSE and BSE Expiry Architecture"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"The expiry calendar is the single most consequential piece of Indian market\r\nstructure for anyone holding options, and it changed substantially between\r\nNovember 2024 and September 2025. Material written before that period describes\r\na market that no longer exists."}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["$","em","em-0",{"children":["Verified 24 July 2026. See ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"docs/learning/README.md"}]," for the full table of\r\nfacts with an expiry date."]}]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The current schedule"}],"\n",["$","table","table-0",{"children":[["$","thead","thead-0",{"children":["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","th","th-0",{}],["$","th","th-1",{"children":"NSE"}],["$","th","th-2",{"children":"BSE"}]]}]}],["$","tbody","tbody-0",{"children":[["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Weekly expiry index"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"NIFTY only"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"SENSEX only"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-1",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Weekly expiry day"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Tuesday"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Thursday"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-2",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Monthly expiry day"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Last Tuesday"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Last Thursday"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-3",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"Stock F&O"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Monthly, last Tuesday"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"—"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"Every NSE derivative contract — index and stock — settles on Tuesday. Every BSE\r\nderivative contract settles on Thursday. The two exchanges were deliberately\r\nseparated onto different days by SEBI so that expiry-day activity is not\r\nconcentrated in a single session across the whole market."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"Why only two indices have weeklies"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"Until November 2024, NSE offered weekly expiries on NIFTY, BANKNIFTY, FINNIFTY,\r\nMIDCPNIFTY and NIFTYNXT50 — an expiry almost every trading day of the week.\r\nBSE offered them on SENSEX, BANKEX and SENSEX 50."}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":["SEBI's November 2024 measures limited each exchange to weekly contracts on\r\n",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"one"}]," benchmark index. NSE retained NIFTY; BSE retained SENSEX. Everything\r\nelse became monthly-only."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":"The rationale was that a near-daily cycle of expiring short-dated options\r\nconcentrated retail activity into the highest-gamma, shortest-dated contracts\r\navailable, where outcomes are most path-dependent and least forgiving."}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":["The practical consequence for anyone holding positions: ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"BANKNIFTY,\r\nFINNIFTY, MIDCPNIFTY and NIFTYNXT50 no longer have weekly options at all."}]," A\r\nposition in those indices is held for weeks, not days, with a correspondingly\r\ndifferent theta and gamma profile. A strategy designed around BANKNIFTY\r\nweeklies does not have an instrument to run on."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Why the day changed"}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":"NSE's expiry sat on Thursday for years. It moved to Tuesday effective September\r\n2025, with BSE simultaneously settling on Thursday. Both exchanges filed their\r\nchoices under a SEBI framework requiring fixed, non-overlapping expiry days."}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":"This matters for anything written from memory or from older material: \"Thursday\r\nexpiry\" is a widely repeated fact about the Indian market that is now wrong for\r\nNSE."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"The holiday rule"}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":["When an expiry day falls on a trading holiday, expiry moves to the ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"previous"}],"\r\ntrading day — not the next one."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":"This is easy to get backwards, and getting it backwards means holding a\r\nposition that has already settled. A Tuesday holiday moves NSE expiry to\r\nMonday; a Thursday holiday moves BSE expiry to Wednesday."}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":"Long weekends compress the effect further: a Monday-Tuesday holiday pair moves\r\nexpiry back to the preceding Friday, shortening the contract by three calendar\r\ndays without changing its label."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"What this changes about holding positions"}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Theta is not uniform across the week."}]," A weekly contract loses extrinsic\r\nvalue fastest in its final sessions. With NIFTY expiring Tuesday, the sharpest\r\ndecay now falls on Monday and Tuesday rather than Wednesday and Thursday."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gamma concentrates on expiry day"}],", which is why SEBI attached an additional\r\n2% extreme loss margin to short option positions on that day and withdrew\r\ncalendar-spread margin benefit for it. See\r\n",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/sebi-derivatives-framework.md"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-14",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Stock and index expiries coincide on NSE."}]," Both settle on the last Tuesday,\r\nso the monthly session carries index cash settlement and stock physical\r\nsettlement simultaneously. Delivery margins on stock positions begin accruing\r\nfour trading days before that date — see\r\n",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/physical-settlement.md"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-15",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Cross-exchange positions settle on different days."}]," A book holding both\r\nNIFTY and SENSEX exposure has two expiry events per week, on Tuesday and\r\nThursday."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/sebi-derivatives-framework.md"}]," — the rules that produced this schedule"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/weekly-vs-monthly.md"}]," — how contract behaviour differs"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"india-market-structure/physical-settlement.md"}]," — what happens to stock contracts at expiry"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/india-market-structure/expiry-architecture.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspac